  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["T6", "T8"],
      "pins": ["T6.1", "T6.2", "T6.3"],
      "nets": ["NET0004 (gate drive)", "ATO_VALVE (drain/NET0015)"],
      "observed": "In the 'ATO Valve' block the low-side switch MOSFET T6 is a 30 V AO3400A (SOT-23), driven through R27 100R/NET0004 with a BT3904 (T7) pre-driver and a 10k pull-up (R40). The 60 V AON6407 that the spec reserves for the valve instead sits in the 'reverse polarity protection' position of the POWER TRAIN (T8).",
      "expected": "The specification's component table assigns the 60 V AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) to the ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch (T3 in the spec's numbering), precisely because it must block the 24 V rail plus solenoid flyback/switching transients. A 30 V part in that position is under-rated.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Page 1 (POWER TRAIN) 'Reverse polarity protection': T8 AON6407; Page 3 'ATO Valve': T6 AO3400A, gate via R27 100R from NET0004, drain to the 24V solenoid load"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch | Netlist: drives ATO_VALVE net; gate driven through R10 (100 Ω), pre-driven via T4 (BT3904)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The ATO valve switch is populated with a 30 V MOSFET on a 24 V inductive load whose turn-off spikes and rail transients (TVS clamps at 28 V) can exceed 30 V, exposing T6 to avalanche stress and premature failure; its higher RdsOn also increases dissipation. The two MOSFETs (AON6407 and AO3400A) appear to have been swapped between the valve and the reverse-polarity positions relative to the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Reference designators in this build are permuted versus the spec's netlist, but the functional blocks still match except for the ATO valve: the spec calls for the 60 V AON6407 there, yet the drawing places a 30 V AO3400A (T6) on the 24 V solenoid switch while the AON6407 (T8) ends up at the reverse-polarity position — an under-rated MOSFET swap that compromises valve reliability."
}

